              "text": "She told him that she had nothing to share, because her own family had very little money and food.",
              "audioStart": 25.125,
              "audioEnd": 30.175
            },
            {
              "text": "However, the wise traveler did not leave, which surprised the woman.",
              "audioStart": 31.038,
              "audioEnd": 34.775
            },
            {
              "text": "He smiled nicely and told her that he could make a wonderful meal using only an ordinary piece of metal.",
              "audioStart": 35.638,
              "audioEnd": 40.875
            },
            {
              "text": "If she would bring him a pot of hot water, a fine dinner would be created right before her eyes.",
              "audioStart": 41.737,
              "audioEnd": 46.5
            },
            {
              "text": "The woman became very curious about this strange idea, so she put a big pot of water over the fire.",
              "audioStart": 47.362,
              "audioEnd": 52.85
            },
            {
              "text": "The traveler dropped the clean iron piece into the hot water and stirred it slowly with a big tool.",
              "audioStart": 53.712,
              "audioEnd": 58.6
            },
            {
              "text": "After a few minutes, he tasted the water.",
              "audioStart": 59.462,
              "audioEnd": 61.862
            },
            {
              "text": "He said that the water was almost ready.",
              "audioStart": 62.725,
              "audioEnd": 64.7
            },
            {
              "text": "He also said that a little bit of salt would make the water better.",
              "audioStart": 65.562,
              "audioEnd": 68.625
            },
            {
              "text": "The woman agreed and brought some salt from her kitchen shelf.",
              "audioStart": 69.487,
              "audioEnd": 72.4
            },
            {
              "text": "Then the traveler suggested that a little piece of potato and some vegetables would transform the water into an absolute celebration.",
              "audioStart": 73.263,
              "audioEnd": 80.125
            },
            {
              "text": "The woman went back into her house and found several nice vegetables that she had kept hidden.",
              "audioStart": 80.987,
              "audioEnd": 85.438
            },
            {
              "text": "More and more pieces were added to the pot as the wise traveler continued to speak with her.",
              "audioStart": 86.3,
              "audioEnd": 90.838
            },
            {
              "text": "Finally, a rich and fine meal was ready for them to enjoy together.",
              "audioStart": 91.7,
              "audioEnd": 95.338
            },
            {
              "text": "The woman was amazed that such a great dinner could be made from almost nothing.",
              "audioStart": 96.2,
              "audioEnd": 100.075
            },
            {
              "text": "She thanked the traveler for his wise plan.",
              "audioStart": 100.938,
              "audioEnd": 103.112
            },
            {
              "text": "She was very happy to share the meal with him.",
              "audioStart": 103.975,
              "audioEnd": 106.15
            },
            {
              "text": "They sat down at the table and ate everything that was in the pot.",
              "audioStart": 107.013,
              "audioEnd": 110.2
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sentences": [
            {
              "text": "The traveler thanked her again before he walked away down the long road.",
              "audioStart": 111.062,
              "audioEnd": 114.513
            },
            {
              "text": "The village people never forgot the man who made a wonderful dinner from almost nothing.",
              "audioStart": 115.375,
              "audioEnd": 119.537
            },
            {
              "text": "Every person in the house talked about the event for many days.",
              "audioStart": 120.4,
              "audioEnd": 123.625
            },
            {
              "text": "The woman learned that sharing could bring great joy to people who had very little.",
              "audioStart": 124.487,
              "audioEnd": 128.275
            },
            {
              "text": "She always remembered the day when the traveler came to her wooden door.",
              "audioStart": 129.137,
              "audioEnd": 132.387
            },
            {
              "text": "Life in the small village continued as before, but people were a little more willing to help one another.",
              "audioStart": 133.25,
              "audioEnd": 138.5
            },
            {
              "text": "The old woman often told the story to her children when they were young.",
              "audioStart": 139.363,
              "audioEnd": 142.75
            },
            {
              "text": "They listened with great interest and asked many questions about the secret metal piece.",
              "audioStart": 143.613,
              "audioEnd": 148.062
            },
            {
              "text": "She always smiled and explained that the pure spirit was the true secret behind the meal.",
              "audioStart": 148.925,
              "audioEnd": 153.363
            },
            {
              "text": "Years passed, and the village grew a little bit larger.",
              "audioStart": 154.225,
              "audioEnd": 157.137
            },
            {
              "text": "New houses were built near the old ones, and more families came to live in the area.",
              "audioStart": 158,
              "audioEnd": 162.4
            },
            {
              "text": "Yet, the story of the traveler remained famous among all the residents.",
              "audioStart": 163.262,
              "audioEnd": 167.037
            },
            {
              "text": "Whenever a stranger walked down the road, people would remember the old woman and her wonderful visitor.",
              "audioStart": 167.9,
              "audioEnd": 172.925
            },
            {
              "text": "They would wonder if the stranger carried something special in his bag.",
              "audioStart": 173.787,
              "audioEnd": 177.088
            },
            {
              "text": "No other traveler ever made a meal from a piece of metal, but the memory lived on.",
              "audioStart": 177.95,
              "audioEnd": 182.175
            },
            {
              "text": "The tradition of sharing food became an important part of life in the village.",
              "audioStart": 183.037,
              "audioEnd": 186.85
            },
            {
              "text": "Families would gather together on cold nights and talk about the great event.",
              "audioStart": 187.713,
              "audioEnd": 191.575
            },
            {
              "text": "The young children grew up knowing that they should always help people who were in need.",
              "audioStart": 192.438,
              "audioEnd": 196.175
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sentences": [
            {
              "text": "The traveler had gone far away, but his wise spirit stayed in the hearts of the local people forever.",
              "audioStart": 197.037,
              "audioEnd": 202.3
            },
            {
              "text": "And so the small village became known as a place where pure support was always shown.",
              "audioStart": 203.162,
              "audioEnd": 207.4
            },
            {
              "text": "This support went to anyone who knocked on a door.",
              "audioStart": 208.262,
              "audioEnd": 210.637
            },
            {
              "text": "Years passed by, and the older generation taught the young children about the great event.",
              "audioStart": 211.5,
              "audioEnd": 216.2
            },
            {
              "text": "If anyone visited the home, they would be welcomed with open arms and simple food.",
              "audioStart": 217.062,
              "audioEnd": 221.338
            },
            {
              "text": "The story spread across the whole country, bringing hope to many families who had very little.",
              "audioStart": 222.2,
              "audioEnd": 226.938
            },
            {
              "text": "People would talk about the wonderful dinner that was created from almost nothing.",
              "audioStart": 227.8,
              "audioEnd": 231.525
            },
            {
              "text": "Even though the traveler was gone, his memory remained strong in every house.",
              "audioStart": 232.387,
              "audioEnd": 236.325
            },
            {
              "text": "The old woman lived for a long time, and she never forgot the special day.",
              "audioStart": 237.188,
              "audioEnd": 241.05
            },
            {
              "text": "Her children grew up and followed her example by helping those who were poor.",
              "audioStart": 241.912,
              "audioEnd": 246.756
            },
            {
              "text": "Whenever winter came, the people gathered together to share warm food and happy stories.",
              "audioStart": 247.618,
              "audioEnd": 252.368
            },
            {
              "text": "They knew that a simple meal could bring people together if everyone shared what they had.",
              "audioStart": 253.231,
              "audioEnd": 257.268
            },
            {
              "text": "The metal piece was kept in a safe place as a reminder of the amazing event.",
              "audioStart": 258.13,
              "audioEnd": 262.143
            },
            {
              "text": "Visitors from distant places often came to hear the story from the older residents.",
              "audioStart": 263.005,
              "audioEnd": 267.168
            },
            {
              "text": "They would look at the wooden door and imagine the traveler standing there.",
              "audioStart": 268.031,
              "audioEnd": 271.33
            },
            {
              "text": "The tradition of sharing became the foundation of life in the small community.",
              "audioStart": 272.193,
              "audioEnd": 275.981
            },
            {
              "text": "No one in the village ever turned away any person who knocked on their door and wanted food.",
              "audioStart": 276.843,
              "audioEnd": 281.243
            },
            {
              "text": "The lesson of the traveler was passed down through many generations of families.",
              "audioStart": 282.106,
              "audioEnd": 286.043
            },
            {
              "text": "And so the simple village remained a symbol of hope and friendship for all time.",
              "audioStart": 286.906,
              "audioEnd": 290.693
            }
          ]
        }
